From: AR0234 port <local>
Subject: [PATCH 0007] vin: fix NULL deref panic in __vin_sensor_setup_link()

Reproduced on the board, ring-buffered on the serial console:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at ... 0000000000000118
  Internal error: Oops: 0000000096000005 [#1] PREEMPT SMP
  Modules linked in: ... vin_v4l2(O) ... [last unloaded: ar0234_mipi(O)]
  CPU: 7 PID: 46474 Comm: vfr
  pc : mutex_lock+0xc/0x54
  lr : media_entity_setup_link+0x24/0x54
  Call trace:
    mutex_lock
    __vin_sensor_setup_link+0xb8/0x124 [vin_v4l2]
    __vin_s_input+0x74/0x3f0 [vin_v4l2]
    vidioc_s_input -> v4l_s_input -> __video_do_ioctl
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal exception

Root cause: the "find the sensor -> mipi/csi media link" loop was

    list_for_each_entry(link, &entity->links, list) {
        if (link->source->entity == entity && link->sink->entity == &subdev->entity)
            break;
    }
    if (link == NULL)
        return -1;

list_for_each_entry() never leaves the cursor NULL - when nothing matches it
points at the list head - so the guard was dead code and the list head was
passed to media_entity_setup_link(). That reads link->graph_obj.mdev out of
whatever the head overlaps and calls mutex_lock() on it, which is the
0x118 / mutex_lock fault above. subdev (the mipi/csi subdev) was also used
without a NULL check.

Trigger: any VIDIOC_S_INPUT (v4l2-ctl, GStreamer, tools/vfr.c, OpenCV) once
the sensor -> mipi link does not exist. That is the normal state after the
sensor module is reloaded, because vin_create_media_links() only builds the
links once, at vin probe time - so

    sudo rmmod ar0234_mipi && sudo modprobe ar0234_mipi
    vfr -t 6 -d /dev/video0            # panics the board, 16s watchdog resets it

is enough. (vin_v4l2 itself cannot be unloaded at all: vin_v4l2 and vin_io
hold references on each other, so `rmmod vin_v4l2` fails with "in use" even
with no stream running and no process holding /dev/video0. HANDOFF 3.1's
"do not rmmod vin after streaming" is about this same reload story.)

Fix: keep the matching link in its own pointer, test that, and reject a NULL
mipi/csi subdev up front with a message instead of crashing.

This is independent of 0005 (which fixed a different NULL deref, one call
later, in sunxi_isp_sensor_type()).
 vin-video/vin_video.c | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
---
--- a/bsp/drivers/vin/vin-video/vin_video.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/vin/vin-video/vin_video.c
@@ -2021,6 +2021,7 @@
 	struct v4l2_subdev *subdev;
 	struct media_entity *entity = NULL;
 	struct media_link *link = NULL;
+	struct media_link *l;
 	__maybe_unused struct sensor_info *info = to_state(sensor);
 	int ret;
 
@@ -2031,14 +2032,46 @@
 		subdev = vind->mipi[vinc->mipi_sel].sd;
 	else
 		subdev = vind->csi[vinc->csi_sel].sd;
+	if (subdev == NULL) {
+		vin_err("sensor %s: no mipi%d/csi%d subdev, cannot link\n",
+			sensor->name, vinc->mipi_sel, vinc->csi_sel);
+		return -1;
+	}
 
+	/*
+	 * list_for_each_entry() leaves the cursor on the list head when nothing
+	 * matches, so it is never NULL and the check below it used to fall
+	 * through with a bogus "link". media_entity_setup_link() then read
+	 * link->graph_obj.mdev out of whatever the list head overlapped and
+	 * called mutex_lock() on that address:
+	 *
+	 *   Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at ... 0x118
+	 *   pc : mutex_lock+0xc/0x54
+	 *   lr : media_entity_setup_link+0x24/0x54
+	 *   __vin_sensor_setup_link+0xb8/0x124 [vin_v4l2]
+	 *   __vin_s_input+0x74/0x3f0 [vin_v4l2]
+	 *   vidioc_s_input -> Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops
+	 *
+	 * Reachable as soon as the sensor -> mipi link does not exist, which is
+	 * the normal state after the sensor module is reloaded (the links are
+	 * only built once, in vin_create_media_links() at vin probe time), so a
+	 * plain `rmmod ar0234_mipi; modprobe ar0234_mipi` followed by any app
+	 * that calls VIDIOC_S_INPUT panicked the board.
+	 * Keep the match in its own pointer instead.
+	 */
 	entity = &sensor->entity;
-	list_for_each_entry(link, &entity->links, list) {
-		if (link->source->entity == entity && link->sink->entity == &subdev->entity)
-				break;
+	list_for_each_entry(l, &entity->links, list) {
+		if (l->source->entity == entity &&
+		    l->sink->entity == &subdev->entity) {
+			link = l;
+			break;
+		}
 	}
-	if (link == NULL)
+	if (link == NULL) {
+		vin_err("sensor %s: no link to %s, cannot (dis)able it\n",
+			sensor->name, subdev->name);
 		return -1;
+	}
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 1, 0)
 	if (info->stream_count >= 1)
 		return 0;
-- 
